    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d723">

                <pb facs="0764" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.852/64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-02T20:00:00-04:00">December 2, 1942—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3784. SD 538 for Rose and Donnelly from Admiral Land.<anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d723-f1"/> Reference our SD 495, Department’s 3703.<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d723-f2"/> You are authorized to <pb facs="0765" n="753"
                        xml:id="pg753"/> supplement previous exchange of notes dated September 30,
                        1942<anchor n="46" xml:id="d723-f3"/> and charter parties signed on October
                    20, 1942 so as to provide as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In consideration of the payment by the owner to the charterer of the sum
                            of $350,000 United States currency the charterer agrees to accept and
                            the owner agrees to deliver to the charterer at ports mutually agreed
                            upon in the United States of America, the following vessels: <hi
                                rendition="#italic">SS Norte Loide, SS Su Loide, SS Vitoria Loide,
                                SS Apa Loide, SS Gavea Loide, SS Pelotas Loide, SS Pirai Loide, SS
                                Rio Loide, SS Baia Loide</hi>.</p>
                        <p>The charterer agrees to make all necessary repairs to said vessels to
                            make the same seaworthy and up to classification as chronicled for in
                            article Nos. 2, 5, 6 of the aforesaid charter parties. It is further
                            agreed that all other terms and conditions of the said charter parties
                            shall remain in full force and effect.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>We do not understand your reference to proviso WSA assume cost of War Risk and
                    total loss insurance. If the reference is intended to mean that Brazilian
                    Government will require same war risk and total loss insurance protection for
                    the period of north bound voyage prior to delivery as they are entitled to
                    receive after delivery we are agreeable to this concession if same absolutely
                    necessary to close transaction although we would prefer not to make the
                    concession if possible. Please proceed accordingly and advise. [Admiral
                    Land.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
